%e A192493 1/2, 1, 5/4, 25/18, 25/16, 2, 5/2, 25/9, 25/8, 13/4, 325/98, 169/50, 65/18, 4, ...
%e A192493 The smallest triangle of lattice points {(0,0),(1,0),(0,1)} has circumradius R=sqrt(2)/2, i.e., R^2=1/2. Therefore a(1)=1, A192494(1)=2.
